{"id":"inspect-dataframe-shape","t":"First-look profile of a table","tags":["Data Processing"],"d":"Easy","rt":"pandas","fn":"table_profile","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":["pandas"],"st":"Before cleaning a new dataset you want four numbers: how big it is and how much of it is missing.\n\nWrite `table_profile(df)` that returns a dict with exactly these keys, each an `int`:\n\n| key | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `rows` | number of rows |\n| `cols` | number of columns |\n| `missing` | number of missing cells (NaN or None) in the whole frame |\n| `complete_rows` | number of rows with **no** missing cell |\n\n## Input\n- `df`: any DataFrame. It may have zero rows; it has at least one column. Text columns may contain `None`, numeric columns may contain `NaN`.\n\n## Example\n```\n   a     b\n0  1.0   x\n1  NaN   y\n2  3.0   None\n```\ngives `{'rows': 3, 'cols': 2, 'missing': 2, 'complete_rows': 1}`.","starter":"import pandas as pd\n\ndef table_profile(df):\n    \"\"\"Return {'rows', 'cols', 'missing', 'complete_rows'} as ints.\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError\n","hints":["`df.shape` is a `(rows, cols)` tuple. `len(df)` is the row count alone.","`df.isna()` returns a boolean frame of the same shape that is True for both NaN and None.","Summing that frame twice (or `.to_numpy().sum()`) counts missing cells. A row is complete when `mask.any(axis=1)` is False. Cast the results to plain `int`."],"sol":"import pandas as pd\n\ndef table_profile(df):\n    rows, cols = df.shape\n    mask = df.isna()                      # True where a cell is NaN or None\n    return {\n        'rows': int(rows),\n        'cols': int(cols),\n        'missing': int(mask.to_numpy().sum()),\n        'complete_rows': int((~mask.any(axis=1)).sum()),\n    }\n","ex_md":"## Why it works\n`df.shape` gives both dimensions at once. `isna()` normalises the two spellings of \"missing\" that pandas uses (`NaN` in float columns, `None` in object columns) into one boolean mask, and every other count is a reduction of that mask: a total sum for `missing`, and a row-wise `any` for incomplete rows.\n\n## Complexity\n$O(R \\cdot C)$ time and one boolean mask of the same size.\n\n## Common bugs\n- `df.size` counts cells, not rows. `len(df.columns)` and `df.shape[1]` are the column count.\n- `df.isna().sum()` is a **per-column** Series. You need a second sum (or `.to_numpy().sum()`) for the grand total.\n- `df.dropna()` drops rows with **any** missing value by default, so `len(df.dropna())` is a valid way to get `complete_rows`; `dropna(how=\"all\")` is not.\n- Returning NumPy integers is fine for the grader, but `json.dumps` and some APIs reject them. Cast with `int(...)`.\n- `df.count()` counts **non-missing** values per column, the complement of what you want.\n\n## Interview follow-ups\n- Which columns would you drop outright, and how do you find them? (`df.isna().mean() > threshold`.)\n- `df.info()` also prints memory use. Why can an object column of short strings use far more memory than an `int64` column, and what does `memory_usage(deep=True)` change?","nex":2,"shown":[{"in":"     a     b\n0  1.0     x\n1  NaN     y\n2  3.0  None","out":"{'rows': 3, 'cols': 2, 'missing': 2, 'complete_rows': 1}"},{"in":"   id name\n0   1    p\n1   2    q\n2   3    r\n3   4    s","out":"{'rows': 4, 'cols': 2, 'missing': 0, 'complete_rows': 4}"}],"lessons":[{"href":"/self-learning-tracks/courses/ai-research-track-web/machine-learning-operations-mlops/data-validation-transformation/","t":"Data Validation & Transformation","c":"AI Research"},{"href":"/self-learning-tracks/courses/ml-toolkit/pandas-for-ml-data/series-dataframes-and-loading-data/","t":"Series, DataFrames and loading data","c":"ML Toolkit"}],"related":["data-types-overview","handle-missing-values"],"ntests":7,"tj":"[{\"a\": [{\"__df__\": {\"columns\": [\"a\", \"b\"], \"data\": [[1.0, \"x\"], [{\"__f__\": \"nan\"}, \"y\"], [3.0, null]]}, \"dtypes\": [\"float64\", \"object\"]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"rows\", 3], [\"cols\", 2], [\"missing\", 2], [\"complete_rows\", 1]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__df__\": {\"columns\": [\"id\", \"name\"], \"data\": [[1, \"p\"], [2, \"q\"], [3, \"r\"], [4, \"s\"]]}, \"dtypes\": [\"int64\", \"object\"]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"rows\", 4], [\"cols\", 2], [\"missing\", 0], [\"complete_rows\", 4]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__df__\": {\"columns\": [\"a\", \"b\"], \"data\": []}, \"dtypes\": [\"float64\", \"object\"]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"rows\", 0], [\"cols\", 2], [\"missing\", 0], [\"complete_rows\", 0]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__df__\": {\"columns\": [\"x\", \"y\"], \"data\": [[{\"__f__\": \"nan\"}, {\"__f__\": \"nan\"}], [{\"__f__\": \"nan\"}, {\"__f__\": \"nan\"}]]}, \"dtypes\": [\"float64\", \"float64\"]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"rows\", 2], [\"cols\", 2], [\"missing\", 4], [\"complete_rows\", 0]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__df__\": {\"columns\": [\"only\"], \"data\": [[null]]}, \"dtypes\": [\"object\"]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"rows\", 1], [\"cols\", 1], [\"missing\", 1], [\"complete_rows\", 0]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__df__\": {\"columns\": [\"v\", \"w\", \"t\"], \"data\": [[1e+300, {\"__f__\": \"nan\"}, \"a\"], [-1e+300, 2.0, null], [0.0, 3.0, \"c\"]]}, \"dtypes\": [\"float64\", \"float64\", \"object\"]}], \"e\": {\"__dict__\": [[\"rows\", 3], [\"cols\", 3], [\"missing\", 2], [\"complete_rows\", 1]]}}, {\"a\": [{\"__df__\": {\"columns\": [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\"], \"data\": [[0.35877340800391416, 1.5106773081434572, -1.7863312373111822, 1.686613508665752, {\"__f__\": \"nan\"}], [-0.7999785843751532, -0.802956718390362, -1.082816516582591, -0.22364535840745078, 0.8338841795521574], [0.5840637316429703, 0.6382860242561829, -1.6948083917690129, -1.5709621176914044, 1.553803174289652], [0.96888536545666, 2.18321400147264, 1.2098158348986146, -1.0243913350545566, 1.2852724548122736], [0.6283942642703312, 0.21482492767891934, -0.8198733225718833, 0.0027802218072239555, {\"__f__\": \"nan\"}], [0.8925351116148221, 0.12449694399871385, 1.5847459143396285, -0.7744857532181485, 0.47110255941042